# Vue – Feature-Sliced Design

Layers (top → bottom):

`app` → `pages` → `widgets` → `features` → `entities` → `shared`

## Import rules

- A layer may import only lower layers
- No upward imports; no cross-feature imports without a public API
- Expose each slice only through its barrel `index.ts`
- Do not import runtime dependencies from `node_modules` outside `shared/api`

## Folders

- `app/` – app shell, providers, global setup
- `pages/` – route/page composition
- `widgets/` – composite UI blocks
- `features/` – user actions (e.g. record a score)
- `entities/` – domain entities (match, athlete, club)
- `shared/` – technical building blocks; UI kit in `shared/ui`

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ Feature uses entity + shared barrels
import { MatchCard } from "@/entities/match";
import { Button } from "@/shared/ui";
import { ref, greet } from "@/shared/api";

// ❌ Direct dependency import
import { invoke } from "@tauri-apps/api/core";
import { ref } from "vue";

// ❌ Entity imports a feature
import { submitScore } from "@/features/scoring";
```

Path alias: `@/` → `src/`
